# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The CHSH game {#the-chsh-game}"
msgstr "Ang CHSH game {#the-chsh-game}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last example to be discussed in this lesson is not a protocol, but a *game* known as the\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huling halimbawa na tatalakayin sa araling ito ay hindi isang protocol, kundi isang *laro* na kilala bilang\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we speak of a game in this context, we're not talking about something that's meant to be played for fun or sport, but rather a mathematical abstraction in the sense of *game theory*.\n"
"Mathematical abstractions of games are studied in economics and computer science, for instance, and they are both fascinating and useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nagsasalita tayo tungkol sa isang laro sa kontekstong ito, hindi tayo nagsasalita tungkol sa isang bagay na nilalaro para sa kasiyahan o palakasan, kundi isang mathematical abstraction sa diwa ng *game theory*.\n"
"Ang mga mathematical abstraction ng mga laro ay pinag-aaralan sa ekonomiya at computer science, halimbawa, at ang mga ito ay parehong kapana-panabik at kapaki-pakinabang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The letters CHSH refer to the authors — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, and Richard Holt — of a 1969 paper where the example was first described.\n"
"They did not describe the example as a game, but rather as an experiment.\n"
"Its description as a game, however, is both natural and intuitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga titik CHSH ay tumutukoy sa mga may-akda — sina John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, at Richard Holt — ng isang papel noong 1969 kung saan unang inilarawan ang halimbawa.\n"
"Hindi nila inilarawan ang halimbawa bilang isang laro, kundi bilang isang eksperimento.\n"
"Ang paglalarawan nito bilang isang laro, gayunpaman, ay parehong natural at intuitive.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game falls within a class of games known as *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Nonlocal games are incredibly interesting and have deep connections to physics, computer science, and mathematics — holding mysteries that still remain unsolved.\n"
"We'll begin the section by explaining what nonlocal games are, and then we'll focus in on the CHSH game and what makes it interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang CHSH game ay nasa loob ng isang klase ng mga laro na kilala bilang *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Ang mga nonlocal game ay hindi kapani-paniwalang kawili-wili at may malalim na koneksyon sa pisika, computer science, at matematika — na nagtataglay ng mga misteryo na hindi pa nareresolba hanggang ngayon.\n"
"Sisimulan natin ang seksyon sa pamamagitan ng pagpapaliwanag kung ano ang mga nonlocal game, at pagkatapos ay tutukuyin natin ang CHSH game at kung ano ang nagpapainteresting nito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Nonlocal games {#nonlocal-games}"
msgstr "Mga nonlocal game {#nonlocal-games}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A nonlocal game is a *cooperative game* where two players, Alice and Bob, work together to achieve a particular outcome.\n"
"The game is run by a *referee*, who behaves according to strict guidelines that are known to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang nonlocal game ay isang *kooperatibong laro* kung saan ang dalawang manlalaro, sina Alice at Bob, ay nagtatrabaho nang magkasama upang makamit ang isang partikular na resulta.\n"
"Ang laro ay pinapatakbo ng isang *referee*, na kumikilos ayon sa mahigpit na mga alituntunin na kilala nina Alice at Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can prepare for the game however they choose, but once the game starts they are *forbidden from communicating*.\n"
"We might imagine the game taking place in a secure facility of some sort — as if the referee is playing the role of a detective and Alice and Bob are suspects being interrogated in different rooms.\n"
"But another way to think about the set-up is that Alice and Bob are separated by a vast distance, and communication is prohibited because the speed of light doesn't allow for it within the running time of the game.\n"
"That is to say, if Alice tries to send a message to Bob, the game will be over by the time he receives it, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring maghanda sina Alice at Bob para sa laro sa anumang paraan na gusto nila, ngunit kapag nagsimula na ang laro, sila ay *ipinagbabawal na makipag-communicate*.\n"
"Maaari nating isipin na ang laro ay nagaganap sa isang uri ng secured na lugar — na parang ang referee ay gumaganap bilang isang detective at sina Alice at Bob ay mga suspek na inuusig sa magkaibang silid.\n"
"Ngunit isa pang paraan upang isipin ang set-up ay ang sina Alice at Bob ay pinaghiwalay ng napakalawak na distansya, at ipinagbabawal ang komunikasyon dahil hindi ito pinahihintulutan ng bilis ng liwanag sa loob ng oras ng pagtakbo ng laro.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, kung susubukan ni Alice na magpadala ng mensahe kay Bob, matatapos na ang laro bago niya ito matanggap, at ganun din.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way a nonlocal game works is that the referee first asks Alice and Bob one question each.\n"
"We'll use the letter $x$ to refer to Alice's question and $y$ to refer to Bob's question.\n"
"Here we're thinking of $x$ and $y$ as being classical states, and in the CHSH game $x$ and $y$ are bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paraan ng pagtakbo ng nonlocal game ay una ay nagtatanong ang referee kina Alice at Bob ng isang tanong bawat isa.\n"
"Gagamitin natin ang titik $x$ para tumukoy sa tanong ni Alice at $y$ para sa tanong ni Bob.\n"
"Dito ay iniisip natin ang $x$ at $y$ bilang mga classical state, at sa CHSH game ang $x$ at $y$ ay mga bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee uses *randomness* to select these questions.\n"
"To be precise, there is some probability $p(x,y)$ associated with each possible pair $(x,y)$ of questions, and the referee has vowed to choose the questions randomly, at the time of the game, in this way.\n"
"Everyone, including Alice and Bob, knows these probabilities — but nobody knows specifically which pair $(x,y)$ will be chosen until the game begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagamit ang referee ng *randomness* para pumili ng mga tanong na ito.\n"
"Nang mas tumpak, may ilang probabilidad na $p(x,y)$ na nauugnay sa bawat posibleng pares $(x,y)$ ng mga tanong, at nangako ang referee na pipiliin ang mga tanong nang random, sa oras ng laro, sa ganitong paraan.\n"
"Lahat, kabilang sina Alice at Bob, ay nakakaalam ng mga probabilidad na ito — ngunit walang sinuman ang partikular na nakakaalam kung aling pares $(x,y)$ ang mapipili hanggang sa magsimula ang laro.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob receive their questions, they must then provide answers: Alice's answer is $a$ and Bob's answer is $b.$\n"
"Again, these are classical states in general, and bits in the CHSH game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos matanggap nina Alice at Bob ang kanilang mga tanong, kailangan nilang magbigay ng mga sagot: ang sagot ni Alice ay $a$ at ang sagot ni Bob ay $b.$\n"
"Muli, ang mga ito ay mga classical state sa pangkalahatan, at mga bit sa CHSH game.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point the referee makes a decision: Alice and Bob either *win* or *lose* depending on whether or not the pair of answers $(a,b)$ is deemed correct for the pair of questions $(x,y)$ according to some fixed set of rules.\n"
"Different rules mean different games, and the rules for the CHSH game specifically are described in the section following this one.\n"
"As was already suggested, the rules are known to everyone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa puntong ito, gumagawa ng desisyon ang referee: sina Alice at Bob ay *mananalo* o *matatalo* depende kung ang pares ng mga sagot $(a,b)$ ay itinuturing na tama para sa pares ng mga tanong $(x,y)$ ayon sa ilang nakatakdang hanay ng mga panuntunan.\n"
"Ang iba't ibang panuntunan ay nangangahulugang iba't ibang mga laro, at ang mga panuntunan para sa CHSH game ay inilarawan sa seksyon kasunod ng ito.\n"
"Tulad ng nabanggit na, ang mga panuntunan ay kilala ng lahat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following diagram provides a graphic representation of the "
"interactions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na diagram ay nagbibigay ng graphical na representasyon ng mga"
" interaksyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is the uncertainty about which questions will be asked, and specifically "
"the fact that each player doesn't know the other player's question, that "
"makes nonlocal games challenging for Alice and Bob — just like colluding "
"suspects in different rooms trying to keep their story straight.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang kawalan ng katiyakan tungkol sa kung aling mga tanong ang itatanong, at "
"partikular ang katotohanan na hindi alam ng bawat manlalaro ang tanong ng "
"kabilang manlalaro, ang nagpapalito sa mga nonlocal game para kina Alice at "
"Bob — tulad ng mga nagkakasabwat na suspek sa magkaibang silid na nagsisikap"
" panatilihing magkaayon ang kanilang kwento.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A precise description of the referee defines an instance of a nonlocal game.\n"
"This includes a specification of the probabilities $p(x,y)$ for each question pair along with the rules\n"
"that determine whether each pair of answers $(a,b)$ wins or loses for each possible question pair $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang tumpak na paglalarawan ng referee ay nagtatakda ng isang instance ng nonlocal game.\n"
"Kabilang dito ang isang detalye ng mga probabilidad na $p(x,y)$ para sa bawat pares ng tanong kasama ang mga panuntunan\n"
"na nagtatakda kung ang bawat pares ng mga sagot $(a,b)$ ay mananalo o matatalo para sa bawat posibleng pares ng tanong $(x,y).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at the CHSH game momentarily, but before that let us briefly acknowledge that it's also interesting to consider other nonlocal games.\n"
"In fact, it's extremely interesting; there are some pretty simple nonlocal games for which it's currently not known how well Alice and Bob can play using entanglement.\n"
"The set-up is simple, but there's complexity at work — and for some games it can be impossibly difficult to compute best or near-best strategies for Alice and Bob.\n"
"This is the surprisingly unintuitive nature of the nonlocal games model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Titingnan natin ang CHSH game sa ilang sandali, ngunit bago iyon ay ilang sandaling kilalanin na kawili-wili rin ang pagtingin sa ibang mga nonlocal game.\n"
"Sa katunayan, napaka-interesante; may ilang medyo simpleng nonlocal game kung saan hindi pa alam kung gaano kahusay ang laro nina Alice at Bob gamit ang entanglement.\n"
"Simple ang set-up, ngunit may kumplikasyon na nagtatrabaho — at para sa ilang mga laro, maaaring imposibleng kalkulahin ang pinakamahusay o malapit sa pinakamahusay na mga estratehiya para kina Alice at Bob.\n"
"Ito ang nakakagulat na hindi-intuitive na katangian ng nonlocal games model.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game description {#chsh-game-description}"
msgstr "Paglalarawan ng CHSH game {#chsh-game-description}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is the precise description of the CHSH game, where (as above) $x$ is "
"Alice's question, $y$ is Bob's question, $a$ is Alice's answer, and $b$ is "
"Bob's answer:\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang tumpak na paglalarawan ng CHSH game, kung saan (tulad ng nasa "
"itaas) ang $x$ ay tanong ni Alice, ang $y$ ay tanong ni Bob, ang $a$ ay "
"sagot ni Alice, at ang $b$ ay sagot ni Bob:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The questions and answers are all bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
msgstr "Ang mga tanong at sagot ay lahat ng mga bit: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee chooses the questions $(x,y)$ *uniformly at random*. That is, "
"each of the four possibilities, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ and $(1,1),$ is "
"selected with probability $1/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinipili ng referee ang mga tanong $(x,y)$ nang *pantay-pantay at random*. "
"Ibig sabihin, bawat isa sa apat na posibilidad, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0),$ "
"at $(1,1),$ ay pinipili na may probabilidad na $1/4.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answers $(a,b)$ *win* for the questions $(x,y)$ if $a\\oplus b = "
"x\\wedge y$ and *lose* otherwise. The following table expresses this rule by"
" listing the winning and losing conditions on the answers $(a,b)$ for each "
"pair of questions $(x,y).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga sagot $(a,b)$ ay *mananalo* para sa mga tanong $(x,y)$ kung "
"$a\\oplus b = x\\wedge y$ at *matatalo* kung hindi. Ang sumusunod na "
"talahanayan ay nagpapahayag ng panuntunang ito sa pamamagitan ng paglilista "
"ng mga kondisyon ng panalo at talo sa mga sagot $(a,b)$ para sa bawat pares "
"ng mga tanong $(x,y).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Limitation of classical strategies {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"
msgstr ""
"Limitasyon ng mga classical na estratehiya {#limitation-of-classical-"
"strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's consider strategies for Alice and Bob in the CHSH game, beginning "
"with *classical* strategies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay tingnan natin ang mga estratehiya para kina Alice at Bob sa CHSH "
"game, simula sa mga *classical* na estratehiya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic strategies {#deterministic-strategies}"
msgstr "Mga deterministikong estratehiya {#deterministic-strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start with *deterministic* strategies, where Alice's answer $a$ is a function of the question $x$ that she receives, and likewise Bob's answer $b$ is a function of the question $y$ he receives.\n"
"So, for instance, we may write $a(0)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $0,$ and $a(1)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsisimula tayo sa mga *deterministikong* estratehiya, kung saan ang sagot ni Alice na $a$ ay isang function ng tanong $x$ na natanggap niya, at gayundin ang sagot ni Bob na $b$ ay isang function ng tanong $y$ na natanggap niya.\n"
"Kaya, halimbawa, maaari nating isulat ang $a(0)$ upang katawanin ang sagot ni Alice kapag ang kanyang tanong ay $0,$ at $a(1)$ upang katawanin ang sagot ni Alice kapag ang kanyang tanong ay $1.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No deterministic strategy can possibly win the CHSH game every time.\n"
"One way to understand this is simply to go one-by-one through all of the possible deterministic strategies and check that every one of them loses for at least one of the four possible question pairs.\n"
"Alice and Bob can each choose from four possible functions from one bit to one bit — which we encountered in the lesson on [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) — and so there are $16$ different deterministic strategies in total to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walang deterministikong estratehiya ang maaaring manalo sa CHSH game sa bawat pagkakataon.\n"
"Isang paraan upang maunawaan ito ay ang simpleng pagtingin sa lahat ng posibleng deterministikong estratehiya nang isa-isa at pagsuri na ang bawat isa sa kanila ay natatalo para sa kahit isa sa apat na posibleng pares ng tanong.\n"
"Maaaring pumili sina Alice at Bob mula sa apat na posibleng function mula sa isang bit patungo sa isang bit — na natuklasan natin sa aralin tungkol sa [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) — kaya mayroon lamang $16$ na iba't ibang deterministikong estratehiya na susuriin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also reason this analytically.\n"
"If Alice and Bob's strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,0),$ then it must be that $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"if their strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,1),$ then $a(0) = b(1);$ and similarly,\n"
"if the strategy wins for $(x,y)=(1,0)$ then $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"So, if their strategy wins for all three possibilities, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari rin tayong mag-isip nang analitiko.\n"
"Kung ang estratehiya nina Alice at Bob ay nanalo kapag $(x,y) = (0,0),$ dapat na $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"kung ang kanilang estratehiya ay nanalo kapag $(x,y) = (0,1),$ kung gayon $a(0) = b(1);$ at gayundin,\n"
"kung ang estratehiya ay nanalo para sa $(x,y)=(1,0)$ kung gayon $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"Kaya, kung ang kanilang estratehiya ay nanalo para sa lahat ng tatlong posibilidad, kung gayon\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the strategy loses in the final case $(x,y) = (1,1),$ and for here winning requires that\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Thus, there can be no deterministic strategy that wins every time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nangangahulugan ito na ang estratehiya ay matatalo sa huling kaso na $(x,y) = (1,1),$ at para manalo dito kinakailangan na\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1).$\n"
"Kaya, walang deterministikong estratehiya ang maaaring manalo sa bawat pagkakataon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is easy to find deterministic strategies that win in three of the four cases, such as $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"From this we conclude that the maximum probability for Alice and Bob to win using a deterministic strategy is $3/4.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kabilang banda, madaling mahanap ang mga deterministikong estratehiya na mananalo sa tatlo sa apat na kaso, tulad ng $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0.$\n"
"Mula dito, nating natukoy na ang pinakamataas na probabilidad para kina Alice at Bob na manalo gamit ang isang deterministikong estratehiya ay $3/4.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic strategies {#probabilistic-strategies}"
msgstr "Mga probabilistikong estratehiya {#probabilistic-strategies}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we just concluded, Alice and Bob cannot do better than winning the CHSH game 75% of the time using a deterministic strategy.\n"
"But what about a probabilistic strategy?\n"
"Could it help Alice and Bob to use randomness — including the possibility of *shared randomness*, where their random choices are correlated?\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng natukoy natin, hindi makapanalo sina Alice at Bob nang higit sa 75% ng oras sa CHSH game gamit ang isang deterministikong estratehiya.\n"
"Ngunit paano ang isang probabilistikong estratehiya?\n"
"Makakatulong ba kina Alice at Bob ang paggamit ng randomness — kabilang ang posibilidad ng *shared randomness*, kung saan ang kanilang mga random na pagpili ay magkakaugnay?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It turns out that probabilistic strategies don't help at all to increase the probability that Alice and Bob win.\n"
"This is because every probabilistic strategy can alternatively be viewed as a random selection of a deterministic strategy, just like (as was mentioned in the [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction) lesson) probabilistic operations can be viewed as random selections of deterministic operations.\n"
"The average is never larger than the maximum, and so it follows that probabilistic strategies don't offer any advantage in terms of their overall winning probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lumabas na ang mga probabilistikong estratehiya ay hindi nakakatulong para mapataas ang probabilidad na mananalo sina Alice at Bob.\n"
"Ito ay dahil ang bawat probabilistikong estratehiya ay maaaring tingnan bilang isang random na pagpili ng isang deterministikong estratehiya, tulad ng (tulad ng nabanggit sa aralin ng [Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction)) ang mga probabilistikong operasyon ay maaaring tingnan bilang mga random na pagpili ng mga deterministikong operasyon.\n"
"Ang average ay hindi kailanman mas malaki kaysa sa maximum, kaya sumusunod na ang mga probabilistikong estratehiya ay hindi nag-aalok ng anumang kalamangan sa mga tuntunin ng kanilang pangkalahatang probabilidad ng panalo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, winning with probability $3/4$ is the best that Alice and Bob can do "
"using any classical strategy, whether deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, ang panalo na may probabilidad na $3/4$ ang pinakamahusay na magagawa "
"nina Alice at Bob gamit ang anumang classical na estratehiya, maging "
"deterministiko o probabilistiko.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game strategy {#chsh-game-strategy}"
msgstr "Estratehiya sa CHSH game {#chsh-game-strategy}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural question to ask at this point is whether Alice and Bob can do any better using a *quantum* strategy.\n"
"In particular, if they share an entangled quantum state as the following figure suggests, which they could have prepared prior to playing the game, can they increase their winning probability?\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang natural na tanong dito: mayroon bang mas magandang estratehiya si Alice at Bob gamit ang *quantum* na pamamaraan?\n"
"Sa partikular, kung magbabahagi sila ng isang entangled quantum state — tulad ng ipinapakita ng sumusunod na figure, na maaari nilang inihanda bago pa maglaro — maaari ba nilang dagdagan ang kanilang probabilidad na manalo?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game-entanglement.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/nonlocal-"
"game-entanglement.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, and this is the main point of the example and why it's so interesting.\n"
"So let's see exactly how Alice and Bob can do better in this game using entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oo, at iyan ang pangunahing punto ng halimbawang ito at kung bakit ito napaka-interesante.\n"
"Kaya tignan natin kung paano eksaktong magagawa ni Alice at Bob na mas mahusay sa larong ito gamit ang entanglement.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Required vectors and matrices {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"
msgstr "Mga kinakailangang vector at matris {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is to define a qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ for each real number\n"
"$\\theta$ (which we'll think of as an angle measured in radians) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang bagay na kailangan nating gawin ay tukuyin ang isang qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle,$ para sa bawat tunay na bilang\n"
"$\\theta$ (na iisipin nating bilang isang anggulo na sinusukat sa radians) tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here are some simple examples:\n"
msgstr "Narito ang ilang simpleng halimbawa:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have the following examples, which arise in the analysis below:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroon din tayong mga sumusunod na halimbawa, na lalabas sa pagsusuri sa "
"ibaba:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Looking at the general form, we see that the inner product between any two "
"of these vectors has this formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag tiningnan ang pangkalahatang anyo, makikita natin na ang inner product"
" ng anumang dalawang vector na ito ay may ganitong formula:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In detail, there are only real number entries in these vectors, so there are no complex conjugates to worry about:\n"
"the inner product is the product of the cosines plus the product of the sines.\n"
"Using one of the *angle addition formulas* from trigonometry leads to the simplification above.\n"
"This formula reveals the geometric interpretation of the inner product between real unit vectors as the cosine of the angle between them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa detalye, ang mga entry ng mga vector na ito ay tunay na bilang lamang, kaya walang complex conjugate na dapat pag-alaralahanin:\n"
"ang inner product ay ang product ng mga cosine kasama ang product ng mga sine.\n"
"Ang paggamit ng isa sa mga *angle addition formula* mula sa trigonometry ay nagdudulot sa simplipikasyon sa itaas.\n"
"Inihahayag ng formula na ito ang geometric na interpretasyon ng inner product sa pagitan ng mga tunay na unit vector bilang cosine ng anggulo sa pagitan nila.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we compute the inner product of the *tensor product* of any two of these "
"vectors with the $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, we obtain a similar "
"expression, except that it has a $\\sqrt{2}$ in the denominator:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung kalkulahin natin ang inner product ng *tensor product* ng anumang "
"dalawang vector na ito kasama ang $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, makakakuha"
" tayo ng katulad na ekspresyon, maliban na may $\\sqrt{2}$ sa denominator:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our interest in this particular inner product will become clear shortly, but"
" for now we're simply observing this as a formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Malilinaw sa ilang sandali kung bakit tayo interesado sa partikular na inner"
" product na ito, ngunit sa ngayon, inoobserbahan lang natin ito bilang isang"
" formula.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, define a unitary matrix $U_{\\theta}$ for each angle $\\theta$ as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, tukuyin ang isang unitary matrix na $U_{\\theta}$ para sa bawat "
"anggulo $\\theta$ tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this matrix transforms $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"To check that this is a unitary matrix, a key observation is that the vectors $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ are orthogonal for every angle $\\theta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa madaling salita, binabago ng matrix na ito ang $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ sa $\\vert 0\\rangle$ at ang $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ sa $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Para matiyak na ito ay isang unitary matrix, ang susi ay ang obserbasyon na ang mga vector $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ at $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ ay ortogonal para sa bawat anggulo $\\theta$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we find that\n"
msgstr "Kaya, natutuklasan natin na\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We may alternatively write this matrix explicitly as\n"
msgstr "Maaari rin nating isulat nang malinaw ang matrix na ito bilang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is an example of a *rotation matrix*, and specifically it rotates two-dimensional vectors with real number entries by an angle of $-\\theta$ about the origin.\n"
"If we follow a standard convention for naming and parameterizing rotations of various forms, we have\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay isang halimbawa ng isang *rotation matrix*, at partikular na iniikot nito ang mga two-dimensional vector na may tunay na bilang na entry sa pamamagitan ng isang anggulo na $-\\theta$ sa paligid ng pinagmulan.\n"
"Kung susundin natin ang isang karaniwang kombensyon para sa pagpapangalan at pagpaparameto ng iba't ibang anyo ng pag-ikot, mayroon tayong\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ kung saan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy description {#strategy-description}"
msgstr "Paglalarawan ng estratehiya {#strategy-description}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can describe the quantum strategy.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon maaari na nating ilarawan ang quantum na estratehiya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Set-up:** Alice and Bob start the game sharing an e-bit: Alice holds a "
"qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the two "
"qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ are in the $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ "
"state.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Paghahanda:** Nagsisimula ang laro habang nagbabahagi si Alice at Bob ng "
"isang e-bit: hawak ni Alice ang isang qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ hawak ni Bob ang "
"isang qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ at magkasama ang dalawang qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ ay nasa $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Alice's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Mga kilos ni Alice:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question $x=0,$ she applies $U_{0}$ to her qubit "
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung matanggap ni Alice ang tanong na $x=0,$ inilalapat niya ang $U_{0}$ sa "
"kanyang qubit $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Alice receives the question  $x=1,$ she applies $U_{\\pi/4}$ to her qubit"
" $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung matanggap ni Alice ang tanong na $x=1,$ inilalapat niya ang "
"$U_{\\pi/4}$ sa kanyang qubit $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The operation Alice performs on $\\mathsf{A}$ may alternatively be described like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ang operasyon na ginagawa ni Alice sa $\\mathsf{A}$ ay maaari ring ilarawan ng ganito:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Alice applies this operation, she measures $\\mathsf{A}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets her answer $a$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pagkatapos ilapat ni Alice ang operasyong ito, sinusukat niya ang "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ gamit ang standard basis measurement at itinatakda ang kanyang"
" sagot $a$ bilang ang kinalabasan ng sukat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Bob's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Mga kilos ni Bob:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=0,$ he applies $U_{\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung matanggap ni Bob ang tanong na $y=0,$ inilalapat niya ang $U_{\\pi/8}$ "
"sa kanyang qubit $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Bob receives the question $y=1,$ he applies $U_{-\\pi/8}$ to his qubit "
"$\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung matanggap ni Bob ang tanong na $y=1,$ inilalapat niya ang $U_{-\\pi/8}$"
" sa kanyang qubit $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Like we did for Alice, we can express Bob's operation on $\\mathsf{B}$ like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Tulad ng ginawa natin para kay Alice, maaari nating ipahayag ang operasyon ni Bob sa $\\mathsf{B}$ ng ganito:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  After Bob applies this operation, he measures $\\mathsf{B}$ with a "
"standard basis measurement and sets his answer $b$ to be the measurement "
"outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pagkatapos ilapat ni Bob ang operasyong ito, sinusukat niya ang "
"$\\mathsf{B}$ gamit ang standard basis measurement at itinatakda ang kanyang"
" sagot $b$ bilang ang kinalabasan ng sukat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit diagram that describes this strategy:\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang isang quantum circuit diagram na naglalarawan ng estratehiyang "
"ito:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/CHSH.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/CHSH.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram we see two ordinary controlled gates, one for $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{\\pi/4}$ on the bottom.\n"
"We also have two gates that look like controlled gates, one for $U_{\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{0}$ on the bottom, except that the circle representing the control is not filled in.\n"
"This denotes a different type of controlled gate where the gate is performed if the control is set to $0$ (rather than $1$ like an ordinary controlled gate).\n"
"So, effectively, Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his qubit if $y=0$ and $U_{-\\pi/8}$ if $y=1;$\n"
"and Alice performs $U_0$ on her qubit if $x=0$ and $U_{\\pi/4}$ if $x=1,$ which is consistent with the description of the protocol in words above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa diagram na ito makikita natin ang dalawang ordinaryong controlled gate, isa para sa $U_{-\\pi/8}$ sa itaas at isa para sa $U_{\\pi/4}$ sa ibaba.\n"
"Mayroon din tayong dalawang gate na mukhang controlled gate, isa para sa $U_{\\pi/8}$ sa itaas at isa para sa $U_{0}$ sa ibaba, maliban na ang bilog na kumakatawan sa control ay hindi puno.\n"
"Ito ay nagtatanda ng ibang uri ng controlled gate kung saan ang gate ay isinasagawa kung ang control ay nakatakda sa $0$ (sa halip na $1$ tulad ng isang ordinaryong controlled gate).\n"
"Kaya, epektibo, ginagawa ni Bob ang $U_{\\pi/8}$ sa kanyang qubit kung $y=0$ at $U_{-\\pi/8}$ kung $y=1;$\n"
"at ginagawa ni Alice ang $U_0$ sa kanyang qubit kung $x=0$ at $U_{\\pi/4}$ kung $x=1,$ na naaayon sa paglalarawan ng protocol sa mga salita sa itaas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to figure out how well this strategy for Alice and Bob works.\n"
"We'll do this by going through the four possible question pairs individually.\n"
msgstr ""
"Natitira na lang na alamin kung gaano kahusay ang estratehiyang ito para kay Alice at Bob.\n"
"Gagawin natin ito sa pamamagitan ng pagtingin sa apat na posibleng pares ng tanong nang isa-isa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case-by-case analysis {#case-by-case-analysis}"
msgstr "Pagsusuri sa bawat kaso {#case-by-case-analysis}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Case 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"
msgstr "Kaso 1: $(x,y) = (0,0).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs "
"$U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr ""
"   Sa kasong ito, inilalapat ni Alice ang $U_{0}$ sa kanyang qubit at ni Bob"
" ang $U_{\\pi/8}$ sa kanya, kaya ang estado ng dalawang qubit "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ pagkatapos nilang isagawa ang kanilang mga "
"operasyon ay\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities for the four possible answer pairs $(a,b)$ are "
"therefore as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ang mga probabilidad para sa apat na posibleng pares ng sagot $(a,b)$ ay "
"kaya ang mga sumusunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We can then obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by "
"summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Maaari tayong makakuha ng mga probabilidad na $a=b$ at $a\\neq b$ sa "
"pamamagitan ng pagdaragdag.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For the question pair $(0,0),$ Alice and Bob win if $a=b,$ and therefore "
"they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para sa pares ng tanong na $(0,0),$ nananalo sina Alice at Bob kung "
"$a=b,$ at samakatuwid nananalo sila sa kasong ito na may probabilidad na\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"

